#AUTO 42
#NEEDED 0
# OTP / eFuse controller recon (issue 110n) — gather once, then de-select.
#
# The non-secure OTP block (0xFE38C000) holds the chip ID / device serial. This
# probe ungates its clock and releases its reset (a read while gated HANGS the
# bus), then reads a status register to confirm the controller is reachable.
#
# The base and clock/reset bits are confirmed against the TRM (Part1 Table 1-1
# + Ch2). The full chip-ID readout is a small state-machine (set user mode,
# address the cpuid word, enable, poll done, read the data register) whose
# control-bit values are NOT in the public TRM (no OTP-controller chapter) —
# they come from Rockchip's driver and are unconfirmed, so this does the safe
# presence read only. See the note in src/019-probe-engine.c (otp_probe). CRU
# clock/reset writes done in C behind a CALL, so no #WRITES needed.

CALL otp_probe
